  "executive_summary": "Treasury's January 2026 foreign-exchange report combines global and partner-country macro surveillance with statutory screening of bilateral trade balances, current-account balances, and persistent one-sided foreign-exchange intervention. For MacroTrace, the reusable content is an external-balance lane linking U.S. domestic demand and exchange rates to imports, exports, capital flows, and partner policy; the statutory thresholds are classification rules, not causal estimates.",
